{#-
  Morpho Blue — supply / withdraw the loan token, and the collateral and
  borrow side of the same markets.

  Singleton is canonical-per-chain, resolved from
  aliases.morpho_blue.singleton (NOT a param). Markets are referenced by
  alias KEY under aliases.morpho_blue.markets. Each market entry must
  declare the full MarketParams tuple:
    loan_token, collateral_token, oracle, irm, lltv
  All five are resolved with no existence guard — a missing key (or a
  missing field on the resolved entry) throws at render time.

  Approves are AUTO-DERIVED from the markets list, deduplicated: the loan
  token always, the collateral token only when `borrow` is on. The Safe only
  needs approve scopes for tokens it can actually hand to the singleton, and
  the markets list already names both, so there is no separate
  `deposit_assets` param. Approves go straight to the addresses pulled from
  the alias entries, bypassing aliases.tokens (the alias registry is already
  the ground truth).

  Required template params:
    markets — list of market alias keys, e.g.
              ["usdc_cbbtc_86", "usdc_wbtc_86", "usdc_wsteth_86"].
              Each entry resolved via aliases.morpho_blue.markets[<key>].
              Duplicate keys are collapsed.
    borrow  — bool. `false` scopes lending only: supply / withdraw of the
              loan token, economically near-neutral and always exitable by
              the Safe alone. `true` additionally scopes supplyCollateral /
              withdrawCollateral / borrow / repay and the collateral-token
              approves.

  `borrow` is required rather than defaulted, deliberately. It gates the
  authority to create debt: a member holding it can post the Safe's whole
  collateral balance and draw to the market LLTV, leaving a position the
  Safe cannot exit without loan-token funds it may no longer hold. A default
  would let every existing config inherit that on the next apply with nobody
  deciding. Required means each config fails to render until a human answers
  the question. It is emitted as a comment in the generated output, both so
  `throwOnUndefined` actually fires when it is missing — that check is on
  emitted VALUES, never on an `{% if %}` — and so the decision is legible in
  the artifact a reviewer reads.

  Resolved from aliases (NOT params):
    aliases.morpho_blue.singleton          — Morpho Blue singleton
    aliases.morpho_blue.markets[<key>]     — MarketParams tuple per market

  Output shape:
    - One approve role per UNIQUE token across both roles, with
      spender = equal_to singleton.
    - One role on the singleton scoping six functions, each with
      marketParams pinned to the configured markets (see the shared
      `market_params` macro). `onBehalf` is pinned to the avatar on all
      six; `receiver` is pinned to the avatar on `withdraw`, `borrow` and
      `withdrawCollateral`, so borrowed assets and released collateral can
      only land back in the Safe.

  Assets vs shares — entry directions pin it, exit directions do not.
  Morpho itself requires exactly one of `assets` and `shares` to be zero
  (`UtilsLib.exactlyOneZero`, Morpho.sol), so pinning one is not about
  preventing an invalid combination; the protocol already does that. It is
  about which of the two the caller has to state.

    Entry — `supply` and `borrow` pin `shares = 0`. Shares-mode would mean
            "deposit (or borrow) whatever assets correspond to N shares",
            so the amount entering or the debt taken on would not be the
            number the caller wrote.
    Exit  — `withdraw` and `repay` leave both `pass`. Shares-mode is the
            only way to leave a position exactly: assets-mode has to name a
            figure derived from an index that moves between the read and the
            transaction, so it either leaves dust or overshoots and reverts.
            Both calls can only unwind the Safe's own position, so admitting
            shares-mode costs nothing. Do not pin these to zero for symmetry
            with the entry pair — it would make a clean exit impossible.

  `data` is left `pass` on supply / supplyCollateral / repay. Morpho fires a
  callback on msg.sender — the avatar Safe — whenever `data` is non-empty,
  and on repay that callback runs AFTER the debt has been reduced and BEFORE
  the Safe has paid.

  That callback is not blocked today; it is answered and ignored. Safe's
  FallbackManager returns `return(0, 0)` for any unknown selector when no
  fallback handler is set (`if iszero(handler)` in FallbackManager.fallback),
  so Morpho's callback succeeds as a silent no-op and the operation
  completes exactly as it would with empty `data`.

  The window is therefore open and merely unoccupied, and what keeps it
  harmless is a property of the SAFE's configuration rather than of this
  policy. A vehicle that installs a fallback handler — ERC-1271 order
  signing wants one — would dispatch Morpho's callback into that handler
  during the repay window, and whether that is safe depends entirely on what
  the handler does. Re-examine this if a handler is ever added. The fork test
  pins both halves, the absent handler and the completing call, so the change
  surfaces as a failing test.

  Length-1 optimization: when `markets` has exactly one entry, the
  marketParams scoping emits a bare `matches` (no `or` wrapper).
  Required because `or` with < 2 conditions is rejected at apply time
  (see the `or` arity check in action/apply/toSdkTargets.ts).
-#}
{%- from "_macros/common.tmpl" import approve -%}
{%- from "_macros/morpho.tmpl" import market_params -%}
{%- set singleton = aliases.morpho_blue.singleton -%}
{#- Pass 1: collapse duplicate market keys. Two identical `or` branches are
    harmless but pointless, and a repeated key would otherwise defeat the
    length-1 optimization below. -#}
{%- set unique_markets = [] -%}
{%- for key in markets -%}
  {%- if key not in unique_markets -%}
    {%- set _ = unique_markets.push(key) -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{#- Pass 2: collect the unique tokens the Safe hands to the singleton. The loan
    token always; the collateral token only when borrowing is on. A token that
    is the loan asset of one configured market and the collateral of another
    must still get exactly one approve entry. -#}
{%- set approved_tokens = [] -%}
{%- for key in unique_markets -%}
  {%- set market = aliases.morpho_blue.markets[key] -%}
  {%- if market.loan_token not in approved_tokens -%}
    {%- set _ = approved_tokens.push(market.loan_token) -%}
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if borrow and market.collateral_token not in approved_tokens -%}
    {%- set _ = approved_tokens.push(market.collateral_token) -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
# borrow: {{ borrow }}
roles:
{%- for token in approved_tokens %}
  {{ approve(token, singleton) | indent(2) }}
{%- endfor %}

  - address: "{{ singleton }}"
    functions:
      - signature: "function supply((address loanToken, address collateralToken, address oracle, address irm, uint256 lltv) marketParams, uint256 assets, uint256 shares, address onBehalf, bytes data)"
        execution_options: "none"
        params:
          - name: marketParams
            param_type: "tuple"
            {{ market_params(unique_markets, aliases) | indent(12) }}
          - name: assets
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "pass"
          - name: shares
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "equal_to"
            value: "0"
            value_type: "uint256"
          - name: onBehalf
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "equal_to_avatar"
          - name: data
            param_type: "dynamic"
            operator: "pass"

      - signature: "function withdraw((address loanToken, address collateralToken, address oracle, address irm, uint256 lltv) marketParams, uint256 assets, uint256 shares, address onBehalf, address receiver)"
        execution_options: "none"
        params:
          - name: marketParams
            param_type: "tuple"
            {{ market_params(unique_markets, aliases) | indent(12) }}
          - name: assets
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "pass"
          - name: shares
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "pass"
          - name: onBehalf
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "equal_to_avatar"
          - name: receiver
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "equal_to_avatar"

{%- if borrow %}
      - signature: "function supplyCollateral((address loanToken, address collateralToken, address oracle, address irm, uint256 lltv) marketParams, uint256 assets, address onBehalf, bytes data)"
        execution_options: "none"
        params:
          - name: marketParams
            param_type: "tuple"
            {{ market_params(unique_markets, aliases) | indent(12) }}
          - name: assets
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "pass"
          - name: onBehalf
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "equal_to_avatar"
          - name: data
            param_type: "dynamic"
            operator: "pass"

      - signature: "function withdrawCollateral((address loanToken, address collateralToken, address oracle, address irm, uint256 lltv) marketParams, uint256 assets, address onBehalf, address receiver)"
        execution_options: "none"
        params:
          - name: marketParams
            param_type: "tuple"
            {{ market_params(unique_markets, aliases) | indent(12) }}
          - name: assets
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "pass"
          - name: onBehalf
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "equal_to_avatar"
          - name: receiver
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "equal_to_avatar"

      - signature: "function borrow((address loanToken, address collateralToken, address oracle, address irm, uint256 lltv) marketParams, uint256 assets, uint256 shares, address onBehalf, address receiver)"
        execution_options: "none"
        params:
          - name: marketParams
            param_type: "tuple"
            {{ market_params(unique_markets, aliases) | indent(12) }}
          - name: assets
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "pass"
          - name: shares
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "equal_to"
            value: "0"
            value_type: "uint256"
          - name: onBehalf
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "equal_to_avatar"
          - name: receiver
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "equal_to_avatar"

      - signature: "function repay((address loanToken, address collateralToken, address oracle, address irm, uint256 lltv) marketParams, uint256 assets, uint256 shares, address onBehalf, bytes data)"
        execution_options: "none"
        params:
          - name: marketParams
            param_type: "tuple"
            {{ market_params(unique_markets, aliases) | indent(12) }}
          - name: assets
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "pass"
          - name: shares
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "pass"
          - name: onBehalf
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "equal_to_avatar"
          - name: data
            param_type: "dynamic"
            operator: "pass"
{%- endif %}
